  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "Differential Scanning Calorimetry (DSC) is the ideal technique for determining melting points and detecting polymorphs, as different crystal forms will exhibit distinct melting temperatures. The TA Instruments DSC250 can perform this analysis, while the TGA can be used alongside it to rule out solvates or thermal degradation. To definitively identify the specific crystal structures of the polymorphs, X-ray Powder Diffraction (XRPD) would be highly recommended, though it is not currently available on the equipment list."
}

