  "not_available": [],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "You can measure the glass-transition temperature of a solid specimen using Dynamic Mechanical Analysis (DMA) on a rheometer. However, you must be aware of a fundamental limitation: heating an acrylic through its Tg will erase its thermal history and may cause it to warp or relax, which will likely alter its mechanical properties for your later tests even if it remains in one piece. If you can safely shave a tiny amount (5-10 mg) from a non-critical area, DSC is the standard alternative that leaves the bulk of the specimen completely unaffected thermally."
}

